WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.100
Dammit!

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.710
Really? You're letting Ebumi play?

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.000
I can't see him doing anything 
other than wreaking more havoc.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:22.390
<b>Episode 9
You've Gotten Stronger</b>

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.650
Hey, #11.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.500
That number you've got there is really mine.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.590
Huh? Hey...

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.090
Ebumi.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.780
I'll play fly-half.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.270
Maroudo, go play center.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.000
Ebumi, you'll be our winger, 
just like you wanted.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.760
I knew I could count on you, Matsu-san.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.870
Ebumi's gone.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.380
Are you feeling lonely?

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:53.820
I...

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.240
I'll practice harder.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.070
I'll get better.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.240
Next time, I'll be standing 
on the field of play.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.420
Good boy. Good boy.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.520
Hey! Don't do that, idiot!

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.750
Don't treat me like a kid!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.740
You'll have to work even harder.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.070
I know that, idiot!

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:14.820
Come on, come on.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.750
I said stop that!

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.760
<i>Some guy who looks like a dumbass
has come out to play.</i>

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.610
Will this work?

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.660
A high punt!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:48.640
I've got it!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.910
Are they going for another kick-off?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.420
Do they even <i>want</i> to go on the offensive?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:08.810
Hana!

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.570
Try!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.810
Wow! I can't believe 
he caught up with that.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.270
He scored a try against Sagami.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.690
You should've warned me you were 
going to kick the ball, Matsu-san.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:37.580
Oh, sorry. I knew you'd get to it, though.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.710
Thanks.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.090
He missed the conversion.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.640
But it's 7-5 now. That might change the mood.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:50.310
Jinko

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:50.310
Sagami

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.320
No one told me Jinko had 
a lightning bolt on their team.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.770
Don't worry about it too much.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.990
Dammit! They got the ball again!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.700
Bastard!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.450
Stay low!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.830
Knock-on by Sagami!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.630
All right!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.130
Their tackling is good.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.100
Ebucchi, go!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.230
It's him again!

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:47.490
He's got a one-on-one 
against Hana on that wing.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.330
Hana, stop him!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.410
Try!

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.020
Hey, first-year.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.620
Make sure your helmet's done up tight.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:32.630
Otherwise, I'll have to be careful 
when I knock you on your ass.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.390
He made the conversion! It's 7-12!

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.240
We've made a comeback!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.050
That was certainly impressive.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:50.620
It's easy to score when you have 
a fast runner on your team.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.090
I thought rugby was a sport 
that was all about teamwork.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:05.430
That's probably how amateurs see it, yes.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:14.440
You guys...

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.700
Do you really think you'll make it
to Hanazono when you can't even crush

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.580
one of Kanagawa's worst teams?

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.560
Don't let him scare you, Hana!

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.930
Y-Yes, sir!

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:35.550
Let's go.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:42.270
Hey, maybe our training camp 
paid off after all!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:47.630
He's so fast!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.860
They're retreating even though
they're on the attack?

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:55.870
Roughing up teams isn't enough by itself
to make them Kanagawa's second-best team.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:00.870
Their real strength lies in how 
solid their fundamentals are...

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.120
Iseyan!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.880
And how high their rugby IQ is.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.880
A-An interception?

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.890
Forwards, come on!

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.220
I'll stop him!

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.980
The first guy was a decoy!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.770
The backs were behind him!

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.770
I can finally stretch my legs!

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.650
Hey, idiot! Don't let them get past you, Suwa!

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.710
Try!

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:59.460
D'you think I should've scored closer 
to the goalposts, Ishibashi-kun?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.770
Yeah. Be more careful next time.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:11.400
That comeback was rather 
short-lived, wasn't it?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:14.030
Jinko

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:14.030
Sagami

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.030
<b>SLAP</b>

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:20.030
<b>Ow! 
Why!?</b>

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.790
Jinko

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:24.720
12-35! That's the end of the first half!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.040
Sagami

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.300
Oh, boy.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.090
You're putting up a good fight.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.010
Yeah, it's not a bad showing.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.890
You've started consciously 
going for lower plays.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.940
You're moving the ball around more.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:55.070
You've gotten stronger.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.730
But Sagami is even stronger.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.010
You're not on their level yet.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.340
You've found something to aim at.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.290
The two tries they scored is 
proof that you're slacking!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.970
You had three missed tackles 
and two missed passes.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.590
At this rate, we'll be 
runners-up again this year!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.810
Go play some proper rugby!

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:22.100
Yes, sir!

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:28.440
What you should be doing right now 
is stealing Sagami's techniques.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.110
They're worth taking.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:38.920
How does Kanagawa's second-best
team pass and run with the ball?

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:43.370
What's their goal when
they're moving the ball around?

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:48.330
If they try to provoke you, steal that, too.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:52.520
It's another way of taking control of a game.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.880
You won't face a more informative team.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.320
Go steal their techniques 
like your lives depend on it!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.270
That's all.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.370
Yes, sir!

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:05.970
Ya-ha!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.090
That's nice and simple! I like it!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.540
Why couldn't you have hurt him sooner?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:24.160
If it wasn't for him, 
we would've made it to Nationals.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.160
Hey, Tree Trunk.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:34.390
You got into a fight during the game.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:40.910
H-He was just being mean to me...

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:43.680
I-I saw red.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.540
You know, I've been thinking...

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:50.180
The way you stand is all wrong.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.440
What?

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.870
I was watching a rugby game
on TV the other day.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:58.940
Huh? What?

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.940
Do this with this.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.210
Yeah, that's it.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.000
You should be standing like this.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.640
Iwashi, you look so strong!

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.910
It'd be even better if you
 tilted your head to the side.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.830
Yeah, like that.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.970
You know what you're talking about, shrimpy.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.520
Iwashi, look down on us more.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.360
People go for you because the way 
you stand makes you look like a weakling.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.800
But...

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.300
Hold your head up high.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.810
After all, you're strong.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:36.750
Iwashi, you look real important!

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:39.320
What are you guys doing?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:46.190
Using banter to take their mind off 
things won't solve anything.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:51.080
They'll still find someone else 
to blame if they lose.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:57.360
Did something happen to you in the past?

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:00.960
It's none of your business.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.430
<i>That winger's the only one 
we have to watch out for.</i>

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.440
I can't believe Hana's 
been so useless this match.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.940
He might get benched for the next game.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.950
Let the second half begin!

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:35.710
Whoops!

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.960
That wasn't much of a tackle.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.770
That hurt.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.930
Don't mess with me, jumbo.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.060
What?

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.530
That's not the right time to use that.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.420
They're resisting,
but they should buckle soon.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.700
I can't catch up!

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:26.790
Hori!

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:29.620
He disappeared?

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.460
You bastard... You can't be serious...

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.460
I scored right between the posts
this time, Ishibashi-kun.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.570
Yeah.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.910
Jinko

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.910
Sagami

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:01.780
It still hurts, dammit.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.360
Why tackle that hard when you know
we're gonna score anyway?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:12.430
<i>One guy pulling off amazing tackles
won't win the game for them.</i>

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.570
Dammit! The ball's moving too fast!

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:32.070
Jeez. Have they finally warmed up?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.580
This is turning into a one-sided game.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.630
<i>I can make it from here!</i>

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.840
Sekizan!

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:01.860
Stop! Stop!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.300
A-Are you okay?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.240
I'm fine.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.250
I'll be right back.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.960
Captain, you okay?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.500
Manager, hurry over here.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:31.020
I've never seen anyone bleed so much before...

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.010
Sheesh.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:39.260
There's a lot of blood,
but the cut's shallow.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:44.310
What's this? You seem awfully happy.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.980
Yeah, because I'm having so much fun.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:53.480
We've got Sagami in our sights now.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.960
We still have time!

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:58.840
Let's score 30 more points!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.370
Yeah!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.060
We'll start with a scrum. Sagami's ball.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.450
Crouch, bind, set!

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:14.700
You're mine!

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.390
You can't stop me with willpower alone!

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:27.650
If one man's not enough...

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.900
get two to tackle them!

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:46.160
If two's not enough, throw three at them!

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.670
Outside! Get the ball outside!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.670
Backs, move up!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.170
Don't give them time to think!

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:01.960
Now...

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:04.560
Now...

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.780
Do whatever it takes!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:09.400
Just knock them down!

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.140
Yeah!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.420
<i>No...</i>

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:20.550
<i>This isn't the Jinko rugby team...</i>

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:25.160
You want me to be the rugby team's adviser?

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.940
I don't even know the rules.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:31.580
That's okay. Nobody does.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.240
They're not a proper club, anyway.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.420
Just so long as they don't get hurt.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.930
<b>Rugby Practice 
Methods</b>

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:43.020
But it'd be rude if I didn't know anything.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:49.690
Jinko

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:49.690
Kawahira

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.150
Let's study harder so we can win next time.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.180
Shut up, Yossen.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:56.940
You don't know anything about rugby.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:00.360
Reading that won't help us now.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:11.130
What? We don't have time to 
teach you the rules, Yossen.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.380
We'll just play by ourselves.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.460
You don't need to get involved.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.490
Hey, it's our adviser! Hello!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.720
He's always so cold.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.500
Score! None of the 
upperclassmen are here.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:58.210
The only good thing about our team 
is all the rugby books we have.

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:05.510
There are ten minutes left
in the second half!

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:12.020
<i>Normally, they'd be smiling.</i>

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:18.020
<i>Wait, when was that?</i>

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.150
<i>How long has it been since I came to a game?</i>

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:28.060
<i>When was the last time 
I actually watched them play?</i>

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.550
<i>When Sekizan and the others 
were first-years...</i>

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.130
Don't underestimate us!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.180
Hey!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.910
Hey! Don't just throw it anywhere!

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.890
Jinko! Go! Go!

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.890
Five more minutes! You can do it!

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.770
Jinko, don't let them beat you!

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.550
<i>Shinshi...</i>

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:01.780
<i>He wasn't that serious about 
the team in his first year...</i>

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:06.780
We haven't lost yet!

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:08.780
We haven't lost yet.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.950
We haven't lost the game yet!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.160
Dammit!

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:22.920
Hey, that was a knock-on!

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.640
How frustrating.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:36.530
Looks like the referee missed it.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:46.740
Crap...

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.880
I'm sorry. I underestimated you at first.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:56.370
This—

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "I Ate Too Much Shaved Ice"</b>

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:49.470
Next time: "I Ate Too Much Shaved Ice."
